  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "Place water in a small saucepan and bring to a boil. Once boiling, add farro and salt, then stir for a few seconds. Reduce heat to low and simmer until farro is tender, 10-15 minutes. When the farro is done, drain and rinse under cold water to cool; set aside to drain further.",
      "secondary_message": "⅓ cup farro, quick-cooking\n¼ tsp salt"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, wash, dry, zest, and juice orange into a large bowl. Add oil, Dijon, vinegar, maple syrup, and spices; whisk to combine the dressing.",
      "secondary_message": "½ orange\n¼ cup extra virgin olive oil\n4 tsp Dijon mustard\n4 tsp white wine vinegar\n4 tsp pure maple syrup\n¼ tsp garlic powder\n¼ tsp salt\n¼ tsp black pepper"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Wash and dry kale. Fold leaves in half lengthwise and slice off the stems; finely chop. Add to the bowl with the dressing. Using your hands, massage kale with the dressing until wilted, 1-2 minutes.",
      "secondary_message": "2 bunch kale"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Add Parmesan, pumpkin seeds, and cranberries to the bowl.",
      "secondary_message": "⅔ cup Parmesan cheese, shredded\n⅓ cup pumpkin seeds\n⅓ cup dried cranberries"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Using the back of a spoon, gently press on the cooked farro to remove excess liquid, then add to the bowl. Toss to combine the salad. ",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Transfer salad to a serving dish and enjoy!",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
